  "name": "claw-orchestrator",
  "description": "Ask Codex, Gemini, Grok or Claude: second opinions, multi-model reviews, background agents, unattended goals. Run and coordinate coding agents on any engine — Claude Code, Codex, Antigravity (Gemini), Grok, OpenCode, ACP agents — from one CLI or MCP server. Use whenever a task is better done by another model, or by more than one: a second opinion or part of the work from Codex, Gemini or Grok; several engines reviewing, analysing, comparing or brainstorming the same thing in parallel (clawo fanout); a coding task handed to a background agent and checked on later; an agent kept working unattended for hours until an objective is met and checked, through usage limits and crashes (clawo goal); a fix or a speed-up proven by checks the agent cannot edit — tests, or a benchmark measured against the commit it started from (clawo solve, acceptance contracts, metric checks, clawo verify); several agents editing one repo in their own worktrees until they agree (council); a careful plan before a big change, or a multi-reviewer code review (ultraplan, ultrareview); an autonomous plan, code and review loop toward a goal (autoloop); a web app built from a short interview (ultraapp); a conversation moved to another engine when one hits its limit (session_handoff); Claude account rotation; cost tracking and spend caps across engines, and which model succeeds more often and at what cost across runs (clawo runs --by model); serving it all to editors over MCP or ACP.",
